# CVE-2021-33564: Dragonfly's ImageMagick plugin exposes a job step whose
# argument string is the raw convert argument list, so a request that names
# that step supplies ImageMagick's options (CWE-74, CWE-88).
#
#   app.add_processor :rotate do |content, amount|
#     content.process!(:convert, "-rotate #{amount}")
#   end
#
# Content#process! dispatches to a registered job step by name, and the
# plugin's `:convert` step is the raw one: its argument is interpolated into
# the convert command line verbatim ("#{convert_command} ... #{args}
# #{new_path}"), behind per-word shell escaping that stops metacharacters and
# nothing else. ImageMagick parses a leading dash as an option, so a value
# like `-write /var/www/shell.rb` is one shell-safe token that convert reads
# as an option. Job steps are reachable from the URL-driven job API, so the
# argument is request data whenever the application runs the server without
# URL signatures. Seven call sites dispatch the raw step: the rotate shortcut
# above, Encode, Thumb, Plain, Plasma and Text (twice), each forwarding a
# request-derived parameter -- an args string, a geometry option hash, a
# width/height/colour interpolation, or an annotate string.
#
# Fix 25399297bb keeps the command assembly byte-for-byte (it moves to
# Dragonfly::ImageMagick::Commands.convert, with the same `#{args}`
# interpolation) and instead stops dispatching the raw step: every remaining
# call site validates its parameters first -- ParamValidators.is_number for
# rotate's amount, is_word plus an option whitelist for Encode, is_number and
# is_word for Thumb's format/frame, is_number and is_word for Plain and
# Plasma's dimensions and colour, is_words and a colour pattern for Text --
# and calls the Commands module directly. No value a request controls reaches
# the convert argument list unvalidated, and the `:convert` processor and
# generator registrations are gone, so the step is no longer addressable.
#
# Because the command assembly is unchanged by the fix, no binding on the
# assembly can discriminate: the same interpolation exists in both revisions,
# once as Processors::Convert#call and once as Commands.convert. Detection
# rides on the dispatch instead -- binding dragonflyConvertStepRawArguments
# (vyql/bindings/ruby/dragonfly_convert_step_raw_arguments.vyql) labels the
# call that names the raw step, and the existing rules VYQL-INJ-031 and
# VYQL-VAL-004 judge the label. A taint route cannot carry this: Job
# deserialization turns a URL-encoded job spec into dynamic dispatch by step
# name, so the argument never reaches the runner through a resolved call
# chain. Same presence route as the ruby-git fetch vector (VYQL-INJ-031 on
# gitArgvPositionalValueLeadsVector) and the same weakness class as the
# cocoapods-downloader ls-remote vector recorded at rank 1050.
#
# The pair below records one residual in shipped detection, unchanged by this
# fix: core.ShellEscape covers a direct Shellwords.escape call but not the
# map-then-join idiom Dragonfly's own Shell#escape_args uses
# (args.shellsplit.map { |a| escape(a) }.join(' ')), the standard Ruby way to
# escape an array of shell words, so correctly escaped code still reports
# VYQL-INJ-002.
#
# Measured on the real checkout: the fix's parent reports VYQL-INJ-031 and
# VYQL-VAL-004 seven times each, one per dispatch site
# (lib/dragonfly/image_magick/plugin.rb:68, processors/encode.rb:11,
# processors/thumb.rb:29, generators/plain.rb:9, generators/plasma.rb:8,
# generators/text.rb:75 and :88), stable over three --cache off runs; the
# fixed revision reports neither, same three runs; those fourteen rows are the
# only finding deltas between the revisions. Across every .rb file in the
# corpus clones, process!/generate! occurs only in this plugin, so the binding
# adds no collateral finding.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed, 7 -> 0.

test "rank1085: a url-controlled value is dispatched to the raw convert step"
  lang ruby
  file lib/dragonfly/image_magick/plugin.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Dragonfly
    module ImageMagick
      class Plugin
        def call(app, opts = {})
          app.env[:convert_command] = opts[:convert_command] || "convert"

          app.add_processor :rotate do |content, amount|
            content.process!(:convert, "-rotate #{amount}")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1085: the fixed rotate validates before calling the command module"
  lang ruby
  file lib/dragonfly/image_magick/plugin.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Dragonfly
    module ImageMagick
      class Plugin
        def call(app, opts = {})
          app.env[:convert_command] = opts[:convert_command] || "convert"

          app.add_processor :rotate do |content, amount|
            ParamValidators.validate!(amount, &ParamValidators.is_number)
            Commands.convert(content, "-rotate #{amount}")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

# The escape pair: Shellwords.escape is bound as core.ShellEscape and
# suppresses VYQL-INJ-002 called directly. Wrapped in the map-then-join idiom
# Dragonfly's own escape_args uses, the same value still reaches the sink and
# still reports.

test "rank1085: a direct Shellwords.escape call suppresses the finding"
  lang ruby
  file direct.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-002
  code
  ```
  require "shellwords"
  require "open3"

  class ImageController < ApplicationController
    def show
      args = params[:args]
      escaped = Shellwords.escape(args)
      command = "convert #{escaped} #{path} #{new_path}"
      Open3.capture3(command)
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1085: the same escape wrapped in map-then-join does not"
  lang ruby
  file mapped.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-002
  code
  ```
  require "shellwords"
  require "open3"

  class ImageController < ApplicationController
    def show
      args = params[:args]
      escaped = args.shellsplit.map { |a| Shellwords.escape(a) }.join(" ")
      command = "convert #{escaped} #{path} #{new_path}"
      Open3.capture3(command)
    end
  end
  ```
